  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Motherhood in Koussan&#xe9;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commune of Koussan&#xe9; (Kayes Region)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Koussan&#xe9;, Mali</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pregnant women may die as a result of complications during and after pregnancy and/or after delivery. Most of these complications can be treated or even avoided. The most common complications causing 75% of maternal deaths are: - Heavy bleeding (especially after childbirth) - Infections (especially after delivery) - Arterial hypertension during pregnancy (preeclampsia and eclampsia) - Complications during childbirth - Unsafe abortions - Other complications are related to diseases such as malaria, diabetes, HIV, etc</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Behaviour Change Communication (SBCC), financial support, increase access to health services</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is that &#x201c; By 2022, maternal and neonatal mortality rate is reduced among 5,577 women of childbearing age in Koussane Commune.&#x201d;</narrative>
  </description>
